          "source": "def-subgaussian-variable-and-vector",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "For $\\sigma^2\\ge0$, a centered real random variable $X$ is **sub-Gaussian with proxy $\\sigma^2$** if $$\\mathbb E e^{\\lambda X}\\le e^{\\lambda^2\\sigma^2/2}\\qquad\\text{for every }\\lambda\\in\\mathbb R.$$",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-conditioning-a-known-variable-and-an-independent-variable",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "if $X$ is $\\mathcal G$-measurable, then $E[X\\mid\\mathcal G]=X$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "def-conditional-expectation-given-a-sigma-algebra",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "A **conditional-expectation version of $X$ given $\\mathcal G$** is a real, $\\mathcal G$-measurable, integrable function $Y$ such that $\\int_A Y\\,dP=\\int_A X\\,dP$ for every $A\\in\\mathcal G$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "lem-conditional-expectation-is-unique-almost-surely",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "If $Y,Z$ are conditional-expectation versions of the same real integrable $X$ given $\\mathcal G$, then $Y=Z$ almost surely.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F6",
          "source": "def-conditional-subgaussian-increments",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "The increments are **conditionally sub-Gaussian around $\\mu$ with proxy $\\sigma^2$** when, for every integer $t\\ge1$ and every fixed $\\lambda\\in\\mathbb R$,",
          "uses": [
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F7",
          "source": "def-gaussian-mixture-confidence-sequence-boundary",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "For $v\\ge0$ define $$u_\\alpha(v):=\\sqrt{(v+\\rho)\\log\\!\\left(\\frac{v+\\rho}{\\alpha^2\\rho}\\right)}.$$",
          "uses": [
            "1.3",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F8",
          "source": "thm-logarithm-derivative-and-integral",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For $x>0$, $\\log$ is differentiable and $$\\log'(x)=\\frac1x,\\qquad \\log x=\\int_1^x\\frac{dt}{t}.$$",
          "uses": [
            "1.3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "A1",
          "source": "def-axiom-of-choice",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "The **Axiom of Choice** (AC) is the following statement.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        }
